```ADD_PAPER
2410.24160v3
This paper introduces CreTok, a novel approach that redefines creativity for diffusion models by incorporating a dedicated token (<CreTok>) into the prompt space. By viewing "creative" as a quantifiable semantic element, the model iteratively samples adaptive and restrictive prompts from a curated dataset (CangJie), then optimizes the similarity between their text embeddings. The paper presents extensive experiments showing that CreTok enables diffusion models to generate outputs that are more diverse, coherent, and original, thereby establishing superior performance in combinatorial and exploratory creative tasks. This work is particularly insightful in demonstrating how meta-prompting can extend the limits of next-token prediction by leveraging multi-token and diffusion-based reasoning, making it highly relevant to the research on algorithmic creativity using minimal open-ended tasks.
``` 
~~~~~~~~~~~
