^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ literature review ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
```ADD_PAPER
2509.02510v1
This work introduces Top-H Decoding, a novel heuristic decoding strategy that dynamically adjusts the model's attention between creativity and coherence. By formulating an entropy-constrained minimization problem, the method rebalances output token probabilities to encourage both originality and logical consistency. Extensive experiments across creative writing and reasoning tasks demonstrate improvements of up to 25.63% over traditional sampling methods in generating diverse yet coherent sequences. The detailed analysis of experimental results highlights that, unlike conventional next-token prediction which is inherently myopic, Top-H Decoding effectively leverages multi-token context and entropy control. These insights are directly aligned with our goal of maximizing algorithmic creativity on minimal open-ended tasks, making this approach a promising candidate for integrating advanced prompt engineering and diffusion-based reasoning techniques.
``` 
~~~~~~~~~~~
