```ADD_PAPER
2509.21474v2
This paper introduces d2, a novel framework that boosts the reasoning ability of diffusion language models by integrating a tailored policy gradient strategy with masked modeling. Rather than relying solely on next-token prediction, d2 leverages multi-token diffusion processes to support iterative, context-aware reasoning. Experimental evaluations on logic puzzles and math reasoning benchmarks demonstrate that d2 not only adapts its computational depth to task complexity but also achieves improved coherence, originality, and diversity in generated outputs. These extensive empirical results highlight how the combination of diffusion-based techniques with reinforcement learning can overcome the inherent myopia of next-token approaches, thereby offering a promising pathway to enhance algorithmic creativity in minimal open-ended tasks.
``` 
~~~~~~~~~~~
