```ADD_PAPER
2308.12059v2
This paper presents a novel approach to prompt engineering that directly manipulates the embeddings in Stable Diffusion-based generators. By treating the prompt as a continuous vector rather than a fixed text string, the method allows for fine-grained control over output attributes, thereby enhancing coherence, originality, and diversity in generated images. Extensive experiments demonstrate that this embedding manipulation technique not only provides improved fidelity and stylistic control compared to traditional next-token prompt generation, but also better supports multi-token and diffusion-based reasoning processes. These empirical results suggest that advanced prompt engineering—which leverages dynamic, multi-token strategies—can more effectively tackle minimal open-ended algorithmic tasks that require combinational and exploratory creativity.
``` 
