```ADD_PAPER
2510.06303v2
This paper introduces SDAR, a novel Synergistic Diffusion-Autoregression paradigm that unifies the strengths of autoregressive models with the parallel inference capabilities of diffusion models for sequence generation. Instead of relying solely on the next-token prediction framework, SDAR leverages a hybrid approach where sequences are generated in blocks through a discrete diffusion process, while overall coherence is maintained via autoregressive chaining. Extensive experiments on scientific reasoning and complex sequence generation tasks (e.g., GPQA and math benchmarks) demonstrate that SDAR not only offers significant speedups and robustness but also overcomes the inherent myopia of next-token prediction by harnessing multi-token processing. These results provide compelling evidence for the benefits of integrating diffusion-based reasoning with traditional autoregressive methods, directly aligning with our objective to maximize algorithmic creativity—enhancing coherence, originality, and diversity—in minimal open-ended algorithmic tasks.
``` 
