Me (Postdoc): Exactly. This pattern insightfully highlights the tradeoffs between memorization and diversity. NTP appears to “play it safe” and essentially reproduces training examples, which we see from the 100% memorization in the null-seed condition. Yet, when we force creative diversity with seed-conditioning or add noise via nonzero temperature, the memorization is rapidly mitigated with a corresponding increase in output uniqueness. MTP and SEDD also show robustness in diversity across similar conditions, but with slightly lower baseline memorization even in deterministic settings.

